{"kind":"report","text":"Technical decision for b56a482f: the proposed internal Node-only object transport is an appropriate next dependency, with the concrete boundaries below. Proceed only after approved layout6d1a1973 has actually landed and exact Main correspondence is checked; approvalf250f501 alone is not that landing. This decision does not supersede the latest archive→Judge/P3 work order or commission premature implementation. The full HistorySource, clone-fetch behavior, CLI/trust/receipt/text decisions and A2/root outcomes remain owed.\n\n1. Keep this first transport private to the Git package, Node-only and read-only, with no new package/barrel export, replay dependency, CLI flag or production caller. Reuse the landed explicit-format IDs/object source and original JournalWork structural budget, not legacy SHA1 repositorySource/nodeExec defaults. The existing nodeExec's1GiB capture remains unchanged; introduce a separate bounded child path. Inputs are an operator-supplied absolute repository directory, fixed native ScopeId/object IDs, original work and downward numeric command/capture options. Bound the repository path to4096UTF8 bytes, reject malformed Unicode/NUL/control characters and option/revision spellings; use argument arrays and never interpolate a shell. Git itself opens the operator-supplied repository/object store; do not claim filesystem confinement of Git's own config/alternates, and do not join any clone-derived tree path to an OS path.\n\n2. Discover storage format once for this transport using bounded git rev-parse --show-object-format=storage. Accept exactly sha1 LF or sha256 LF, without trim-based permissiveness, compatibility-ID translation or ID-length inference. Unsupported Git capabilities or other output fail closed as unavailable/format; no quiet SHA1 fallback. Use only this chosen storage format to validate full lowercase nonzero IDs. Current local Git is2.54.0 Apple Git-157; do not silently raise package engine/platform requirements. The storage option is documented by [Git rev-parse](https://git-scm.com/docs/git-rev-parse).\n\n3. Resolve only journalRef(validated native ScopeId), not an arbitrary ref string or prefix listing. Use exact ref plumbing without abbreviation, pattern enumeration, revision syntax or tag dereference. Require a direct archive ref in this initial cohort: a bounded symbolic-ref -q --no-recurse check may reject a symbolic ref without following its chain; status1 means nonsymbolic,128 is lookup failure. Then show-ref --exists distinguishes absent2 from other lookup failure1; an existing ref is read with show-ref --verify --hash -- \u003cexact ref\u003e, accepting exactly one selected-format ID plus LF. A ref disappearing between commands is unavailable, not a verified absent history. The returned ID is an unpeeled Git object name, not a commit/head/incarnation proof; the caller's JournalObjectReader and later source must establish those. Document/retest these statuses on supported Git; alternatives need identical exact/missing/error semantics. References: [symbolic-ref](https://git-scm.com/docs/git-symbolic-ref), [show-ref](https://git-scm.com/docs/git-show-ref).\n\n4. object(id,limit) validates a natural safe limit, downward from8MiB and the same work's per-object ceiling, before commands. A zero-limit call is metadata ONLY even for an empty object: never launch a nonempty body command. Probe one exact ID through cat-file --batch-check with an explicit fixed objectname/objecttype/objectsize format and exactly one ID+LF input. Accept only a closed ASCII record with that exact ID, supported archive type and canonical safe decimal size, or the exact ID missing LF result. No blank/extra fields/lines/CR/BOM, filtering, rev syntax, all-object enumeration, mailmap, text conversion or symlink following. Metadata may report an oversized object's size without allocating/reading its body. If size exceeds the requested positive limit, return metadata with data:null; do not start a body. For an admitted body, freeze ID/type/size across the await, use raw cat-file \u003csupported type\u003e \u003cfull ID\u003e, cap stdout at the admitted exact size, require that exact byte count and return an owned intrinsic Uint8Array copy. Empty bodies may return an owned empty array from the valid metadata alone. A changed/malformed envelope or body is object-mismatch. Actual content hash validation remains mandatory in the existing JournalObjectReader; the transport is not a second authority or hash certificate. A ref to a tag is never peeled into a commit. Raw content and missing-record behavior are documented by [cat-file](https://git-scm.com/docs/git-cat-file).\n\n5. Use the existing complete allowlisted hardened environment/config principles, never ambient Git config env/credentials. Keep no-replace and no-lazy-fetch enabled, no prompts/hooks/fsmonitor/attributes helpers, no pager, and no optional writes/locks. Fixed built-in commands only; no aliases, external Git subcommands, filters, textconv, credential helper, remote-object-info or implicit fetch. This read-only path must not opt into GitProgram's local/HTTPS transport permissions: prohibit network/protocol fallback here and preserve legacy runner behavior elsewhere. Git documents no-replace/no-lazy-fetch/no-optional-locks explicitly in its [2.54 command reference](https://git-scm.com/docs/git/2.54.0). Fail unsupported capabilities closed rather than retrying with protections disabled.\n\n6. Publish command capture limits before work: metadata/format/ref stdout\u003c=1024bytes and stderr\u003c=1024bytes; body stdout\u003c=its exact admitted size\u003c=8MiB and stderr\u003c=1024. Check each stream and their sum before retaining/copying a chunk; reaching exactly the cap may succeed, crossing it cannot. No decode/concatenate-before-limit check or1GiB execFile buffer. One active child per transport, no unbounded internal queue; overlapping use refuses limit rather than spawning additional children. Options only lower these caps/30,000ms child wall limit, never raise them or replace the original deadline.\n\nConcrete initial charging: before each command let A be a conservative bounded argv/stdin byte reservation (three times argv UTF16 code-unit count plus stdin's intrinsic bytes is acceptable). Spend calls1, reserve metadata2048+A through work.metadata, and reserve inputWork256+A+2*(stdoutCap+stderrCap) through work.input. Before retaining EACH chunk spend additional metadata64 for chunk bookkeeping; both streams count, including cached/repeated/failed commands and zero-byte process replies. Reserve owned concatenation/copies within those2passes; any extra pass/copy adds its own charge first. Close/destroy streams at refusal; never hold an excess chunk just to construct an error. The downstream reader's probe/copy/hash/parse reservations remain additional, not transferred or refunded. Publish actual remaining availability: double validation/copy work and many commands may stop below8MiB/512attempts. Never reset/enlarge4096/512/64/16384/4MiB/64MiB/original30s to fit a fixture. This is bounded app capture/work, not a child-process/OS whole-heap or physical-preemption claim.\n\n7. Run each child under the SAME budget.wait and a downward child timer. Own its cancellation handle outside the awaited operation so original-budget rejection can request termination immediately. At ANY budget/capture/timeout failure latch the first reason, discard partial stdout/stderr, cancel stdin/output consumption and request child termination. Late data/exit/error/close events may clean up but cannot resolve success, populate a cache or start another command. A terminal transport refuses subsequent calls without launching a child. Recheck the original budget at completion before returning owned bytes. Do not wait indefinitely for an uncooperative child's close event before refusing the caller, and do not call kill acknowledgment proof of physical cancellation.\n\nError mapping: genuine exact missing-object record=\u003enull; exact absent-ref status=\u003enull. Original budget limit/timeout/unavailable reasons propagate unchanged. Capture overflow or downward work/command-size exhaustion=\u003eterminal limit; own child timer=\u003eterminal timeout. Spawn/IO/nonzero exit/signal/unsupported Git/lookup failure=\u003eunavailable, never missing. Unsupported storage label=\u003eformat; malformed ID/input=\u003eobject-id/input before launch; malformed metadata/unsupported object shape/wrong raw byte count=\u003eobject-mismatch. A wrong hash is object-mismatch at JournalObjectReader, never accepted Git integrity. Discard stderr and untrusted output in returned messages; fixed reason/step/code only. Do not invent later HistorySource mismatch/trust/receipt reports in this transport.\n\nRequired focused witnesses: actual local clones in both formats that really carry the custom ref using an explicit mirror/refspec fixture; exact ID resolution without peeling, absent/direct/symbolic/corrupt cases and unrelated refs untouched; loose and packed raw object reads, size0/probe/at-cap/over-cap, malformed metadata, unsafe argument spellings, owned buffers; partial-clone missing objects with fetching/config execution/replacement/filter paths disabled. Mark scripted process faults separately from real subprocess behavior. Cover both streams, many small chunks/bookkeeping exhaustion, failed launches/exits, child and original timeouts, late events and no subsequent launch/partial success. Include one focused distinguishing control at an actual output/forbidden-body/original-deadline boundary; a generic unrelated rejection is inconclusive. Then one frozen gate and complete exact Source review after the layout landing; do not repeat the layout gate or substitute a P3 composition result.\n\nBasis read: fullb56a/cc72e736 preparation (adopted78a141ac), durability15.7, actual complete Node/GitProgram/repositorySource implementation, package exports/engine and journal-ref grammar, HistorySource allowance interfaces, ordinary CLI clone argv, plus official Git command references above. Two initial guessed source filenames did not exist; the actual program.ts and commands.ts locations were read instead. No Source edit, package/lock change, installation, test/gate, provider call, push, deployment or publication was performed for this decision. This supplies a concrete first dependency only; it neither closes A2 nor narrows its HistorySource/clone/trust/receipt/text/integrity/replay witnesses, asynchronous writer/privacy/consent/disclosure, G1 certificate/at-send retention or root outcomes.","body":{"formal_approval":"false","no_git_artifact":"true","promise":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:ac23fa9ed5b947c599e816a83425660f5dcfd9a8","request":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b56a482fa5ee62a63642756a3e607f8bf7682fd3"}}